---
title: Baked Ziti
description: Baked ziti with Italian sausage in a tomato-cream sauce, layered with mozzarella and pecorino.
tags: [pasta, casserole, make-ahead]
course: main
icons: [sausage, cheese-swiss, pan-food]
cuisine: Italian
source:
  name: Once Upon a Chef
  url: https://www.onceuponachef.com/recipes/baked-ziti-with-sausage.html
servings: 8
prep time: 40m
cook time: 50m
---

= Noodles

Bring a large #pot{} of salted water to a boil. Add the @ziti noodles{1%lb} and cook according to the package directions for very al dente, about ~boil{7%minutes}. (It will continue to cook in the oven, so you want to undercook it just a bit.) Drain and add the pasta back to the pot. Set aside.

= Sauce

Preheat the oven to 425°F (220°C) and set the oven rack in the middle position.

Heat a large #sauté pan{} (preferably nonstick) over medium-high heat. Crumble the @Italian sausage{1 1/2%lb}(ground spicy or sweet, or removed from casings) into the pan and cook, breaking it apart with a #wooden spoon{}, until lightly browned and just cooked through, ~cook{5-6%minutes}. Use a #slotted spoon{} to transfer the cooked sausage to a plate.

Drain all but 1 tablespoon of the fat from the pan and set over low heat (if you don't have enough fat in the pan, add a tablespoon of olive oil). Add the @garlic cloves{4}(minced) and cook, stirring constantly with the wooden spoon, until soft but not browned, about ~cook{1%minute}.

Add the @crushed tomatoes{1%can}(28 oz), @salt{1%tsp}, @sugar{1 1/2%tsp}, and @red pepper flakes{1/4%tsp} and simmer, uncovered, for ~simmer{10%minutes}.

Add the @heavy cream{1%cup}, 1/3 cup of the @pecorino Romano cheese{1/3%cup}(grated, or Parmigiano Reggiano), the cooked sausage, and the @fresh basil{1/3%cup}(chopped, plus more for serving) to the pan; stir until evenly combined.

Carefully pour the contents of the sauté pan into the large pot with the pasta and gently stir to combine.

= Bake

Spoon half of the mixture into a 9-by-13-inch #baking dish{}. Sprinkle with half of the @whole milk mozzarella cheese{113%g}(1 cup, shredded) and half of the remaining @&pecorino Romano cheese{1 1/2%tbsp}.

Spoon the remaining pasta mixture on top and sprinkle with the remaining @&whole milk mozzarella cheese{113%g} and @&pecorino Romano cheese{1 1/2%tbsp}.

Transfer to the oven and bake, uncovered, until the cheese has melted and browned, ~bake{15-20%minutes}. Sprinkle with more basil and serve.

> **Making ahead** — The dish can be assembled, covered, and refrigerated for up to 2 days in advance, or frozen for up to 3 months. (If frozen, defrost in the refrigerator overnight.) Whether refrigerated or frozen and defrosted, bake, covered tightly with aluminum foil, in a 425°F (220°C) oven for 25 minutes. Then uncover and bake for another 10 to 15 minutes, until the cheese is lightly browned and the pasta is hot throughout.
